  "id": "COMPOUND:38271 - PROTEIN:5790",
  "verbalization": "Sasanquasaponin I appears to have multiple targets that ultimately lead to a relationship with HPAC, suggesting a complex network of interactions. The evidence indicates that Sasanquasaponin I may inhibit microtubule-associated protein 1B, which is a target of 6-hydroxy-2-[2-(2-hydroxyphenyl) ethyl]chromone and CID 11603911, both of which target HPAC. Similarly, Sasanquasaponin I may also interact with Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, which is targeted by N-Methyltyramine, also leading to HPAC. These findings suggest that Sasanquasaponin I may act through multiple pathways, potentially modulating cellular processes that influence HPAC activity. The integration of these targets implies that Sasanquasaponin I could exert its effects through diverse mechanisms, possibly involving enzyme inhibition or protein modification, which may contribute to its interaction with HPAC. The evidence supports a plausible mechanistic link, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
